WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.604
RustGIS v0.8.0 keeps

00:00:03.522 --> 00:00:04.465
every layer in

00:00:04.277 --> 00:00:05.479
its native coordinate

00:00:05.291 --> 00:00:05.998
system

00:00:06.534 --> 00:00:08.067
The pure-Rust open-source

00:00:07.878 --> 00:00:09.269
GIS for desktop

00:00:09.329 --> 00:00:10.543
web and mobile

00:00:10.355 --> 00:00:11.982
merges 300 +

00:00:11.829 --> 00:00:12.984
pull requests from

00:00:12.796 --> 00:00:14.057
20 contributors

00:00:14.246 --> 00:00:15.413
adding native per-layer

00:00:15.225 --> 00:00:16.097
projections

00:00:16.192 --> 00:00:17.253
picture markers

00:00:17.289 --> 00:00:18.574
chart layouts and

00:00:18.397 --> 00:00:19.800
new network analysis

00:00:20.326 --> 00:00:21.222
Layers are now

00:00:21.034 --> 00:00:21.764
drawn

00:00:21.906 --> 00:00:23.580
measured analyzed and

00:00:23.392 --> 00:00:24.229
saved in their

00:00:24.041 --> 00:00:25.455
own coordinate systems

00:00:25.279 --> 00:00:27.212
using PROJ 9.9

00:00:27.734 --> 00:00:28.995
Data stays local

00:00:28.854 --> 00:00:29.691
unless you send

00:00:29.503 --> 00:00:30.033
it to a

00:00:29.845 --> 00:00:31.059
model you choose

00:00:31.198 --> 00:00:32.577
RustGIS is a

00:00:32.389 --> 00:00:33.721
fast free and

00:00:33.616 --> 00:00:35.136
open-source GIS in

00:00:34.948 --> 00:00:35.891
pure Rust for

00:00:35.703 --> 00:00:36.422
mapping

00:00:36.575 --> 00:00:38.143
analyzing and sharing

00:00:37.955 --> 00:00:39.228
geospatial data

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:40.764
Full story on

00:00:40.575 --> 00:00:41.471
the dashboard
